RASK-INIT-PLACEHOLDER

This is not the real rask-init binary. The real one is a linux/arm64
executable produced at build time by:

    make rask-init

(or the equivalent pre hook in .goreleaser.yml's darwin build), which builds
github.com/sivchari/rask/cmd/rask-init through raskinit/go.mod.

It exists so that //go:embed has something to embed, and so `go build ./...`
works on a fresh checkout. Only macOS clusters read it: rask boots it as PID 1
inside the VM. Linux clusters never do -- rask runs the control plane as host
processes there.
